-- title:
--   Finite group actions on colorings
-- statement:
--   Let a group $G$ act on a position set $D$, and let $C$ be a color set. A coloring fixed by $g\in G$ is identified with a function from the position orbits of the cyclic subgroup generated by $g$ to $C$. Colorings carry the action $(g\cdot f)(d)=f(g^{-1}\cdot d)$. The definitions also give the translation action $k\cdot x=k+x$ on $\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z$, written with the additive group in multiplicative notation, together with its transitivity and cancellation properties. This action is defined for every natural $n$; finite counting applications impose a nonzero modulus separately.
